---
description: Bound browser page evaluation and stop after a timeout
alwaysApply: true
---

When using the browser tool, never call `Runtime.evaluate` or `page.evaluate` without a 5-second timeout. If it times out, do not retry the same call. Take a screenshot, check for a paused debugger or an open dialog, reload the page, and report what happened before continuing.

Pass the timeout on the call itself:

```json
{
  "method": "Runtime.evaluate",
  "params": {
    "expression": "...",
    "timeout": 5000
  }
}
```

A timeout means the page is stuck, not that the expression needs another attempt. After reporting the screenshot, debugger or dialog state, and reload, choose a different check or stop.
